---
title: DeskFlow — SLA & Escalation Flow
---
sequenceDiagram
    participant Sched as SLACheckerScheduler<br/>(every 60 s)
    participant SLAS as SLAService
    participant Kafka as Apache Kafka
    participant EC as EscalationEventConsumer
    participant ES as EscalationService
    participant NS as NotificationService
    participant DB as PostgreSQL
    participant WS as WebSocket

    loop Every 60 seconds
        Sched->>DB: query OPEN/IN_PROGRESS/PENDING_CUSTOMER tickets
        DB-->>Sched: ticket list with sla_deadline

        loop For each ticket
            Sched->>SLAS: checkTicket(ticket)

            alt now > deadline - warning_hours AND not warned
                SLAS->>Kafka: publish sla.warning {ticketId, priority, deadline}
                Kafka->>NS: SLAWarningEvent consumed
                NS->>DB: persist Notification (SLA_WARNING)
                NS->>WS: push to agent /user/queue/notifications
            else now > deadline AND not escalated
                SLAS->>DB: ticket.escalated = true
                SLAS->>Kafka: publish sla.breached {ticketId, priority, agentId}

                Kafka->>EC: SLABreachedEvent consumed
                EC->>ES: escalate(ticketId)
                ES->>DB: find available Supervisor (round-robin)
                ES->>DB: create EscalationLog
                ES->>Kafka: publish escalations.created {ticketId, supervisorId}

                Kafka->>NS: EscalationCreatedEvent consumed
                NS->>DB: persist Notification (ESCALATION) for Supervisor
                NS->>DB: persist Notification (ESCALATION) for Agent
                NS->>WS: push to supervisor /user/queue/notifications
                NS->>WS: push to agent /user/queue/notifications
                NS->>NS: sendEmail(supervisor, escalation details)
            end
        end
    end